18:["$","aside",null,{"className":"docs_toc__B_lbZ","aria-label":"On this page","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"ON THIS PAGE"}],[["$","a","protect-simultaneous-edits",{"href":"#protect-simultaneous-edits","children":"Protect simultaneous edits"}],["$","a","keep-the-process-healthy-too",{"href":"#keep-the-process-healthy-too","children":"Keep the process healthy too"}],["$","a","diagram-compare-a-version-before-saving",{"href":"#diagram-compare-a-version-before-saving","children":"Diagram: compare a version before saving"}],["$","a","implementation-enforce-ownership-where-the-effect-occurs",{"href":"#implementation-enforce-ownership-where-the-effect-occurs","children":"Implementation: enforce ownership where the effect occurs"}],["$","a","engineering-exercise",{"href":"#engineering-exercise","children":"Engineering exercise"}],["$","a","design-review-questions",{"href":"#design-review-questions","children":"Design review questions"}],["$","a","read-further",{"href":"#read-further","children":"Read further"}]]]}]
19:["$","main",null,{"className":"docs_main__7o2m6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"docs_articleMeta__8zYHO","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"LESSON 09 OF 10"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Systems"}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"docs_article__Ja_Vh","children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":[[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"Concurrency, locks, and runtime health"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Concurrency"}]," means work overlaps in time. The difficult case is not just many readers; it is two editors changing the same document or two processes claiming the same maintenance job. A ",["$","strong","strong-1",{"children":"race condition"}]," exists when the outcome depends on timing that the design has not controlled."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"id":"protect-simultaneous-edits","children":"Protect simultaneous edits"}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":["Both editors read version 7. Alice saves first; Bob saves afterward. A blind ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"UPDATE"}]," loses Alice's edit. With ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"optimistic concurrency"}],", Bob submits the version he read:"]}],"\n",["$","pre","pre-0",{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-sql","children":"UPDATE documents\nSET title = $new_title, version = version + 1\nWHERE id = $id AND version = 7;\n"}]}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":["If the affected-row count is zero, return a conflict and show the current version; do not silently overwrite. This fits conflicts that are relatively rare. ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Pessimistic locking"}]," reserves the row while a short transaction computes a change, useful when conflicts are common or a multi-step invariant needs protection. Keep lock order consistent and transactions short to reduce ",["$","strong","strong-1",{"children":"deadlocks"}],"; on deadlock or serialization failure, retry the ",["$","em","em-0",{"children":"whole"}]," transaction only when the operation is safe to retry."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":"A distributed lock coordinates processes, but a lock lease can expire while a paused holder is still working. For a critical effect, use a fencing token or a storage-level conditional write so an old holder cannot act after a new leader. Leader election identifies one coordinator; it does not magically make its effects exactly once."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"id":"keep-the-process-healthy-too","children":"Keep the process healthy too"}],"\n",["$","p","p-4",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Thread safety"}]," means shared in-memory state behaves correctly under concurrent execution. Avoid mutable global request state; protect shared structures or keep state local. A ",["$","strong","strong-1",{"children":"memory leak"}]," is memory that remains reachable but is no longer useful, such as unbounded in-memory document caches or event listeners never removed. Garbage collection reclaims unreachable objects, not objects a mistaken cache still references. Watch heap growth, GC pause time, allocation rate, and p99 latency under sustained load; restart policies only hide a leak temporarily."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"id":"diagram-compare-a-version-before-saving","children":"Diagram: compare a version before saving"}],"\n",["$","figure","p-5",{"className":"docs_studyFigure__4Js_y","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"docs_studyFigureViewport__ZYDNN","children":["$","img","img-0",{"className":"docs_studyFigureImage__Gb2YJ","src":"/learning/scale-design/concurrency.svg","alt":"Two editors read version seven; Alice's conditional update creates version eight and Bob's stale update is rejected with a conflict.","width":"920","height":"402","loading":"lazy"}]}],"$L25"]}],"\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e","\n","$L2f","\n","$L30","\n","$L31"],false]}]]}],"$L32"]}]
