2a:["$","p","p-7",{"children":["Use the SQL conditional ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"UPDATE ... WHERE id = $id AND version = $expected"}]," from this lesson as the final authority for edits; check ",["$","code","code-1",{"children":"row_count === 1"}],". If a Redis lease protects a scheduled cleanup job, include a monotonically increasing fencing token in writes to the downstream store or make the write conditional there. A lock key alone cannot prevent a paused old holder from resuming. Set a bounded in-process cache size and test steady-state heap after repeated document reads; a garbage collector cannot reclaim still-referenced entries."]}]
